{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1519654996,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMDAyNTY4NTU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2228","origin":"github"},"title":"`remove` should remove metadata?","message":"Boils down to a conceptual decision. If we remove a direct subdataset, should `remove` remove the aggregate metadata for it too. if so, then any remove requires a traversal upwards to adjust superdataset content beyond the `save` of the subdataset change (which it is already recording).\n\nIf we do it for datasets, what about files? If we do it for files, we would have to re-aggregate on remove of a single file. Which changes the state of the dataset, hence flags reaggregation in any superdataset.\n\nI don't think this would be wise....","files":null}]}